  "captionUrl": "https://content.jwplatform.com/tracks/ZJ95Pl3X.srt",
  "rawCaptions": "1\n00:00:00,031 --> 00:00:02,859\nHello and welcome to your guide on getting started with Claude.\n\n2\n00:00:03,339 --> 00:00:06,006\nMy name is Stephen Grider and I am a member of Technical Staff\n\n3\n00:00:06,147 --> 00:00:08,835\nat Anthropic. In this video, I'm going to give you a quick\n\n4\n00:00:08,935 --> 00:00:11,522\nintroduction of the course. I'll help you understand what topics\n\n5\n00:00:11,541 --> 00:00:14,148\nwe'll be covering, requirements to get through the course, and I'll\n\n6\n00:00:14,169 --> 00:00:16,695\ngive you some tips on how to succeed. We are going\n\n7\n00:00:16,734 --> 00:00:19,417\nto cover a wide variety of topics throughout the course.\n\n8\n00:00:19,437 --> 00:00:21,960\nWe'll first begin with some background on models offered by\n\n9\n00:00:22,019 --> 00:00:24,562\nAnthropic, then quickly move into understanding how to\n\n10\n00:00:24,702 --> 00:00:27,704\naccess them through the official Anthropic API. From\n\n11\n00:00:27,745 --> 00:00:30,448\nthere, we'll focus on prompting, first with evaluations,\n\n12\n00:00:30,788 --> 00:00:33,310\nthen engineering techniques. Next up, we'll be a\n\n13\n00:00:33,390 --> 00:00:36,213\ndeep dive on expanding Claude's capabilities through tool\n\n14\n00:00:36,232 --> 00:00:38,795\nuse. We will understand how to get task-specific\n\n15\n00:00:38,935 --> 00:00:41,677\ncontext into Claude with retrieval augmented generation,\n\n16\n00:00:42,078 --> 00:00:44,600\nthen focus on connecting Claude to new services with\n\n17\n00:00:44,640 --> 00:00:47,264\nmodel context protocol. We'll walk through\n\n18\n00:00:47,283 --> 00:00:50,009\ntwo agents created by Anthropic, named Claude Code\n\n19\n00:00:50,170 --> 00:00:52,774\nand Computer Use, and understand how to apply them to solve\n\n20\n00:00:52,814 --> 00:00:55,399\ninteresting problems. Finally, we'll spend some time\n\n21\n00:00:55,460 --> 00:00:58,545\nto learn how to handle more complex tasks with workflows\n\n22\n00:00:58,646 --> 00:01:01,351\nand agents. There's a lot of content to cover here,\n\n23\n00:01:01,671 --> 00:01:04,216\nso there are a couple of expectations on your side\n\n24\n00:01:04,257 --> 00:01:06,862\nto make sure that we can get through everything. First,\n\n25\n00:01:07,003 --> 00:01:09,509\nyou need to have a basic understanding of Python, along\n\n26\n00:01:09,528 --> 00:01:12,254\nwith a Python environment that can run notebooks. The\n\n27\n00:01:12,295 --> 00:01:15,001\nvast majority of code in this course will be written into and\n\n28\n00:01:15,162 --> 00:01:17,748\nexecuted from notebooks. You will also\n\n29\n00:01:17,787 --> 00:01:20,594\nneed access to the Anthropic API, which will require\n\n30\n00:01:20,715 --> 00:01:23,802\neither an Anthropic account or an API key.\n\n31\n00:01:23,781 --> 00:01:26,426\nI will provide directions later on to help you get an\n\n32\n00:01:26,525 --> 00:01:29,129\nAPI key. Lastly, given the speed at which\n\n33\n00:01:29,189 --> 00:01:31,694\nwe'll cover different topics, I do have some tips to\n\n34\n00:01:31,733 --> 00:01:34,237\nhelp you find success. First, I highly\n\n35\n00:01:34,278 --> 00:01:36,861\nrecommend you write code alongside me. Watching\n\n36\n00:01:36,900 --> 00:01:39,424\nsomeone else author code isn't really enough to absorb it.\n\n37\n00:01:40,286 --> 00:01:42,890\nSecond, consider speeding up the video playback speed in\n\n38\n00:01:42,909 --> 00:01:45,513\nthe video player that you are using. This will help you get through\n\n39\n00:01:45,534 --> 00:01:48,058\nthe content at a faster pace and make it easier\n\n40\n00:01:48,097 --> 00:01:51,442\nto review specific videos that you might find challenging.\n\n41\n00:01:51,793 --> 00:01:54,376\nThird, you've got to apply some of the techniques that you learn\n\n42\n00:01:54,438 --> 00:01:57,260\nthroughout the course. Consider expanding or altering\n\n43\n00:01:57,301 --> 00:01:59,965\nthe different notebooks that we author. Fourth,\n\n44\n00:02:00,165 --> 00:02:02,709\nif you get stuck at any point in time, ask Claude for\n\n45\n00:02:02,769 --> 00:02:05,832\nhelp. Claude can get you unstuck from just about any situation\n\n46\n00:02:06,093 --> 00:02:09,377\nor clarify points that you might find confusing. Well,\n\n47\n00:02:09,538 --> 00:02:12,181\nthat's enough of an introduction for now, so let's start learning about\n\n48\n00:02:12,241 --> 00:02:13,582\nClaude in the next video.",
  "transcriptText": "Hello and welcome to your guide on getting started with Claude.\n\nMy name is Stephen Grider and I am a member of Technical Staff\n\nat Anthropic. In this video, I'm going to give you a quick\n\nintroduction of the course. I'll help you understand what topics\n\nwe'll be covering, requirements to get through the course, and I'll\n\ngive you some tips on how to succeed. We are going\n\nto cover a wide variety of topics throughout the course.\n\nWe'll first begin with some background on models offered by\n\nAnthropic, then quickly move into understanding how to\n\naccess them through the official Anthropic API. From\n\nthere, we'll focus on prompting, first with evaluations,\n\nthen engineering techniques. Next up, we'll be a\n\ndeep dive on expanding Claude's capabilities through tool\n\nuse. We will understand how to get task-specific\n\ncontext into Claude with retrieval augmented generation,\n\nthen focus on connecting Claude to new services with\n\nmodel context protocol. We'll walk through\n\ntwo agents created by Anthropic, named Claude Code\n\nand Computer Use, and understand how to apply them to solve\n\ninteresting problems. Finally, we'll spend some time\n\nto learn how to handle more complex tasks with workflows\n\nand agents. There's a lot of content to cover here,\n\nso there are a couple of expectations on your side\n\nto make sure that we can get through everything. First,\n\nyou need to have a basic understanding of Python, along\n\nwith a Python environment that can run notebooks. The\n\nvast majority of code in this course will be written into and\n\nexecuted from notebooks. You will also\n\nneed access to the Anthropic API, which will require\n\neither an Anthropic account or an API key.\n\nI will provide directions later on to help you get an\n\nAPI key. Lastly, given the speed at which\n\nwe'll cover different topics, I do have some tips to\n\nhelp you find success. First, I highly\n\nrecommend you write code alongside me. Watching\n\nsomeone else author code isn't really enough to absorb it.\n\nSecond, consider speeding up the video playback speed in\n\nthe video player that you are using. This will help you get through\n\nthe content at a faster pace and make it easier\n\nto review specific videos that you might find challenging.\n\nThird, you've got to apply some of the techniques that you learn\n\nthroughout the course. Consider expanding or altering\n\nthe different notebooks that we author. Fourth,\n\nif you get stuck at any point in time, ask Claude for\n\nhelp. Claude can get you unstuck from just about any situation\n\nor clarify points that you might find confusing. Well,\n\nthat's enough of an introduction for now, so let's start learning about\n\nClaude in the next video.",
  "downloads": []
